    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1182">

                <pb facs="1231" n="1219" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/3–945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-09T19:00:00+02:00">March 9, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>331. The Yugoslav Ambassador<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1182-f1"/> informed me today
                    that he had learned from a reliable source that subsequent to the Yalta
                        Conference,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1182-f2"/> Molotov<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d1182-f3"/> had informed the Turkish Ambassador in Moscow<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d1182-f4"/> that the Soviet Government would desire soon to
                    discuss with the Turkish Government a revision of the Montreux
                        Convention.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d1182-f5"/> The Turkish Ambassador is said
                    to have replied that the Montreux Convention “was an international matter”.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated to Moscow as No. 12.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1182-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1182-f1-content">
                <p>Iliya Shumenkovich.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1182-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1182-f2-content">
                <p>The Yalta Conference between President Roosevelt, British Prime Minister
                    Churchill, and Chairman of the Council of People’s Commissars of the Soviet
                    Union Stalin met February 4–February 11, 1945; see <ref target="frus1945Malta">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, The Conferences at Malta and
                        Yalta, 1945</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1182-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1182-f3-content">
                <p>Vyacheslav Mikhailovich Molotov, People’s Commissar for Foreign Affairs of the
                    Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1182-f4" n="4" xml:id="d1182-f4-content">
                <p>Selim Sarper.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1182-f5" n="5" xml:id="d1182-f5-content">
                <p>Signed July 20, 1936, League of Nations Treaty Series, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">clxxiii</hi>, p. 213; for documentation on the
                    interest of the United States in the Montreux Conference regarding the regime of
                    the Straits, June 22–July 20, 1936, see <ref target="frus1936v03#pg_503">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1936, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 503</ref> ff.; for documentation
                    concerning discussion of the Montreux Convention at Yalta, see <ref
                        target="frus1945Malta#pg_328">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Conferences at Malta and Yalta</hi>, pp.
                        328</ref>–<ref target="frus1945Malta#pg_329">329</ref>, <ref
                        target="frus1945Malta#pg_903">903</ref>–<ref target="frus1945Malta#pg_904"
                        >904</ref>, and <ref target="frus1945Malta#pg_982">982</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
